title=\"58-df-zfc-descriptive2-standard-borel-space\">58-df-zfc-descriptive2-standard-borel-space</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\">\\(S\\)</span> (ambient formal setting)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E,X,\\mathcal B_X\\in V\">\\(E,X,\\mathcal B_X\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{\\mathcal N}\">\\(\\tau_{\\mathcal N}\\)</span> (the canonical Baire-space topology defined below)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{StandardBorelSpace}\">\\(\\operatorname{StandardBorelSpace}\\)</span> (standard-Borel-space predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B(Y,\\tau)\">\\(\\mathcal B(Y,\\tau)\\)</span> (Borel sigma-algebra, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"9375de7089953a2b\" href=\"?note=9375de7089953a2b\" title=\"58-df-borel\">58-df-borel</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EquivRel}\">\\(\\mathrm{EquivRel}\\)</span> (equivalence-relation predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"1a891abf5fe2909c\" href=\"?note=1a891abf5fe2909c\" title=\"58-df-equivalence\">58-df-equivalence</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> (set-function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcDescriptive2SmoothEquivalenceRelation}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcDescriptive2SmoothEquivalenceRelation}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}descriptive2\\text{-}smooth\\text{-}baire\\text{-}topology}\\vdash\n\\tau_{\\mathcal N}\\coloneqq\\Bigl\\{U\\subseteq\\omega^\\omega:\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall y\\in\\omega^\\omega\\;(y\\upharpoonright n=x\\upharpoonright n\\to y\\in U)\\Bigr\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}descriptive2\\text{-}smooth\\text{-}baire\\text{-}topology}\\vdash\n\\tau_{\\mathcal N}\\coloneqq\\Bigl\\{U\\subseteq\\omega^\\omega:\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall y\\in\\omega^\\omega\\;(y\\upharpoonright n=x\\upharpoonright n\\to y\\in U)\\Bigr\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}descriptive2\\text{-}smooth\\text{-}equivalence\\text{-}relation} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcDescriptive2SmoothEquivalenceRelation}_S(E,X,\\mathcal B_X)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{StandardBorelSpace}(X,\\mathcal B_X)\\land\\mathrm{EquivRel}(E,X)\\land\\exists f\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(f,X,\\omega^\\omega)\\land\\forall C\\in\\mathcal B(\\omega^\\omega,\\tau_{\\mathcal N})\\;(f^{-1}[C]\\in\\mathcal B_X)\\land\\forall x,y\\in X\\;(\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in E\\leftrightarrow f(x)=f(y))\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}descriptive2\\text{-}smooth\\text{-}equivalence\\text{-}relation} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcDescriptive2SmoothEquivalenceRelation}_S(E,X,\\mathcal B_X)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{StandardBorelSpace}(X,\\mathcal B_X)\\land\\mathrm{EquivRel}(E,X)\\land\\exists f\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(f,X,\\omega^\\omega)\\land\\forall C\\in\\mathcal B(\\omega^\\omega,\\tau_{\\mathcal N})\\;(f^{-1}[C]\\in\\mathcal B_X)\\land\\forall x,y\\in X\\;(\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in E\\leftrightarrow f(x)=f(y))\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Smoothness is a Borel reduction of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E\">\\(E\\)</span> to equality on Baire space.</li>\n<li>The Baire-space Borel algebra is derived from an explicit canonical topology, so the three-argument predicate has no hidden free parameter <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B_{\\omega^\\omega}\">\\(\\mathcal B_{\\omega^\\omega}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The function graph, measurable-preimage condition, and equivalence relation use sourced formal predicates.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-ax-zfc]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-equivalence","status":"resolved","id":"1a891abf5fe2909c","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-equivalence]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-borel","status":"resolved","id":"9375de7089953a2b","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-borel]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-zfc-descriptive2-standard-borel-space","status":"resolved","id":"3169dc41990b4bbe","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-zfc-descriptive2-standard-borel-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-borel","status":"resolved","id":"9375de7089953a2b","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathcal B(Y,\\tau)$ (Borel sigma-algebra, see [[58-df-borel]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-equivalence","status":"resolved","id":"1a891abf5fe2909c","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{EquivRel}$ (equivalence-relation predicate, see [[58-df-equivalence]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Function}$ (set-function predicate, see [[58-df-function]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"S","display":false},{"tex":"E,X,\\mathcal B_X\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_{\\mathcal N}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{StandardBorelSpace}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal B(Y,\\tau)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{EquivRel}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcDescriptive2SmoothEquivalenceRelation}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}descriptive2\\text{-}smooth\\text{-}baire\\text{-}topology}\\vdash\n\\tau_{\\mathcal N}\\coloneqq\\Bigl\\{U\\subseteq\\omega^\\omega:\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall y\\in\\omega^\\omega\\;(y\\upharpoonright n=x\\upharpoonright n\\to y\\in U)\\Bigr\\}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}descriptive2\\text{-}smooth\\text{-}equivalence\\text{-}relation} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcDescriptive2SmoothEquivalenceRelation}_S(E,X,\\mathcal B_X)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{StandardBorelSpace}(X,\\mathcal B_X)\\land\\mathrm{EquivRel}(E,X)\\land\\exists f\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(f,X,\\omega^\\omega)\\land\\forall C\\in\\mathcal B(\\omega^\\omega,\\tau_{\\mathcal N})\\;(f^{-1}[C]\\in\\mathcal B_X)\\land\\forall x,y\\in X\\;(\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in E\\leftrightarrow f(x)=f(y))\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"E","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal B_{\\omega^\\omega}","display":false}],"bytes":2230,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1817","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch06/58-df-zfc-descriptive2-smooth-equivalence-r